From a9d865c16f2500bd96e05bccd79e38f062f0e691 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zubon2003 <zubon2003@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 22:03:43 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] c5-fpga-hdmi UART link build (not an official C5VRX release)

Modification of C5VRX-5 v5.0.523 (96995500) for the c5-fpga-hdmi FPGA
receiver, which takes the MODEM_DIAG IQ and does not use the analog
output:

- IQ pins back on the header as in v5.0.387: Q sign on D3/GPIO7 and
  I bit 0 on D10/GPIO10 instead of GPIO2 and the user-LED GPIO27 (#263),
  so the FPGA wiring stays the same.
- UART1 at 115200 8N1 on XIAO D4 = GPIO23 (TX) and D5 = GPIO24 (RX), the
  two DAC LSB pins, which are no longer driven. Only the keys b (next
  band), c (next channel), s (scan) and ? (report now) are taken from it;
  it answers "CH <name> <MHz>" + CR LF on every channel change and once a
  second.
- Internal RAM is nearly full on this release: a link task made the gain
  observer's xTaskCreate fail at boot (ESP_ERR_NO_MEM). The link has no
  task of its own (the console task polls it), keeps only the minimum RX
  ring and no TX ring, and starts after the receiver tasks.

C5VRX by Twotoz and the C5VRX contributors, GPL-3.0-only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
